course: dictionary
lesson: 5162
title: Irritable: cross, or sore?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Irritable means easily annoyed or made angry. Someone who is grumpy at the slightest thing is irritable. Read the clues in the sentence: «Screens late at night make it harder to fall asleep, and children who sleep too little learn less and are more irritable (easily cross).» The brackets tell you the meaning straight away: easily cross.
explain: The sentence also gives you a cause. Children who sleep too little become irritable, so tiredness can make a person cross. People can also get irritable when they are hungry or ill. Try your meaning in the sentence: «children who sleep too little learn less and are more easily cross». It still makes sense, so you have got it.
explain: Irritable has a second meaning in medicine. It means sore or sensitive, as in «irritable skin». Skin that is irritable is easily hurt or upset by things like soap or wool. The word is the same, but the context tells you which meaning to use.
fact: Irritable means easily annoyed or made angry; grumpy.
fact: «Irritable» is an adjective, and its comparative is «more irritable».
fact: Phrases to remember: feel irritable, get irritable.
fact: In medicine, irritable means sore or sensitive, as in «irritable skin».
fact: Words with more than one meaning are checked by their context: the sentence around the word tells you which meaning fits.
exercise: «Children who sleep too little are more irritable (easily cross).» What does irritable mean here? | *Easily annoyed or cross | Full of energy and singing | Bright and shiny | Very tired and fast asleep
exercise: Mum says, «You are being irritable because you are hungry.» What does irritable suggest? | Quiet and sleepy | Happy and excited | *Grumpy and easily annoyed | Hungry for cake only
exercise: In a health lesson, «irritable skin» means skin that is what? | *Sore or sensitive | Cold to the touch | Painted in bright colours | Shiny and smooth
test: Jo is tired and snaps at her brother over nothing. Which word best describes Jo? | Happy | Ancient | Luminous | *Irritable
test: A doctor says the rash has made the skin irritable. What does irritable mean here? | Full of sparkles | *Sore or sensitive | Dry and cracked from the sun | Easily cross
exam: Why might a child feel irritable after a bad night's sleep? | *They are tired and easily annoyed | They have just won a prize | They have eaten a huge feast | They are glowing like a lamp
